Q: stop BR tag breaking with CSS A: <p>Following on the answers here, this prevents the <code>&lt;br&gt;</code> tag breaking in both Chrome and IE.  It does NOT add a space automatically as CSS cannot do that.  A space <em>could</em> be potentially emulated with padding or similar but would be janky at best.  See comments below.</p>
<pre><code>br {
    content: &quot; &quot;;
    display: none;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Want to test two PHP installs, updating from 7.4 to 8.0 A: <p>You need Apache to send each virtual host to the right PHP-FPM socket or port. Changing the <code>listen</code> port in <code>www.conf</code> alone is not enough; Apache still needs a matching <code>SetHandler</code>/<code>ProxyPassMatch</code> rule.</p>
<p>For example, with PHP-FPM listening on <code>127.0.0.1:9801</code> for PHP 7.4 and <code>127.0.0.1:9803</code> for PHP 8.0:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;VirtualHost *:80&gt;
    ServerName old-site.local
    DocumentRoot /var/www/old-site/public

    &lt;Directory /var/www/old-site/public&gt;
        AllowOverride All
        Require all granted
    &lt;/Directory&gt;

    &lt;FilesMatch \.php$&gt;
        SetHandler &quot;proxy:fcgi://127.0.0.1:9801&quot;
    &lt;/FilesMatch&gt;
&lt;/VirtualHost&gt;

&lt;VirtualHost *:80&gt;
    ServerName upgrade-test.local
    DocumentRoot /var/www/upgrade-test/public

    &lt;Directory /var/www/upgrade-test/public&gt;
        AllowOverride All
        Require all granted
    &lt;/Directory&gt;

    &lt;FilesMatch \.php$&gt;
        SetHandler &quot;proxy:fcgi://127.0.0.1:9803&quot;
    &lt;/FilesMatch&gt;
&lt;/VirtualHost&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Then add local hostnames:</p>
<pre><code>127.0.0.1 old-site.local
127.0.0.1 upgrade-test.local
</code></pre>
<p>On Windows that goes in:</p>
<pre><code>C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts
</code></pre>
<p>Restart both PHP-FPM services and Apache, then create a small test file in each site:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php phpinfo();
</code></pre>
<p>Open:</p>
<pre><code>http://old-site.local
http://upgrade-test.local
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>phpinfo()</code> output should show PHP 7.4 on one and PHP 8.0 on the other.</p>
<p>Cloudflare Tunnel is unrelated for local testing unless you specifically want to expose the test site externally. The key part is routing each Apache vhost to the intended PHP-FPM listener.</p>

Q: How to change the position of a gif? A: <p>I think you're missing here is <code>* { margin: 0; padding: 0}</code> setting every elements' padding and margin to 0.</p>
<p>So, it will not show any white space.</p>
<p>Apart from that, you can apply <code>position: relative;</code> to parent and <code>position: absolute</code> and left, right, top or bottom positions.</p>
<p>Hope this helps.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>* {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="magpie"&gt;
  &lt;img src="https://media.giphy.com/media/v1.Y2lkPTc5MGI3NjExYWx5a2NlNHpwMHdlZ296aGg4enliODd3N2NtazJ2NDY3MDIxbng4byZlcD12MV9naWZzX3NlYXJjaCZjdD1n/2xpXiYRJHOjCiquX1C/giphy.gif" height="500px" alt="a drawing of an australian magpie moving side to side"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Vim keyboard shortcut to move around tabs A: <p><kbd>g</kbd>+<kbd>t</kbd> and <kbd>g</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd> are Vim's shortcuts to jump to next &amp; previous tabs.</p>
<p>You can use <code>&lt;C-Tab&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;C-S-Tab&gt;</code> to map within Vim but you'll probably need to help your <strong>terminal</strong> produce correct key codes. Depending on your terminal,</p>
<p><strong><a href="http://software.schmorp.de/pkg/rxvt-unicode.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">urxvt</a></strong>, add to your <code>.Xresources</code> file:</p>
<pre><code>URxvt*keysym.C-Tab:    \033[27;5;9~
URxvt*keysym.C-S-Tab:  \033[27;6;9~
</code></pre>
<p><strong><a href="https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty" rel="nofollow noreferrer">kitty</a></strong>, add to your <code>~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf</code>:</p>
<pre><code>map ctrl+i send_text all \x1b[27;5;105~
map ctrl+tab send_text all \x1b[27;5;9~
map ctrl+shift+tab send_text all \x1b[27;6;9~
</code></pre>
<p><strong><a href="https://github.com/jwilm/alacritty" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Alacritty</a></strong>, add following to your <code>~/.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-ini prettyprint-override"><code>[[keyboard.bindings]]
chars = &quot;\\u001B[27;5;105~&quot;
key = &quot;I&quot;
mods = &quot;Control&quot;

[[keyboard.bindings]]
chars = &quot;\\u001B[27;5;9~&quot;
key = &quot;Tab&quot;
mods = &quot;Control&quot;

[[keyboard.bindings]]
chars = &quot;\\u001B[27;6;9~&quot;
key = &quot;Tab&quot;
mods = &quot;Control|Shift&quot;
</code></pre>
